Dear colleges,

We update our system clock using NTP server, we disable the daylight saving
at the zoneinfo table and build (using zic) a new localtime image.
The problem is that know on when time changes (according to the daylight
change time) at the NTP server,  the time all the servers update but doesn't
turn on/off the daylight saving "flag" at the system.
The major problem here is that the daylight saving changes every year and
it's not set always to the same date.
Updating and compiling and synchronizing quit a lot of servers is not an
easy job

For example :
using the command date on non daylight saving time will display : Tue Oct 17
18:00:33 IST 2000
at daylight saving we will get : Tue Oct 17 18:00:33 IDT 2000
The difference between the two above is with the "D" and "S".

more seriously at the tm struct :  inittm_isdst (that indicate if we on
daylight or not) is not change accordingly.

using the NTP time updates we lost this option, and the time is set with the
IST always.

Is there an option to set the system daylight flags w/out using the zoneinfo
tables ?
Does the NTP servers can set this flags ?
How can we on the other hand synchronize clocks and keep using NTP ?

The major problem here is that the daylight saving changes every year and
it's not set always to the same date.
Updating and compiling and synchronizing quit a lot of servers is not an
easy job, that's why we use NTP.

Thanks in advance,
Ran Zahor






