Date: 2000/10/23
Message-ID: <yyzr957q57y.fsf@geri.mjolner.dk>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 684733924
X-Complaints-To: usenet@daimi.au.dk
X-Trace: gjallar.daimi.au.dk 972293138 5722128 130.225.8.27 (23 Oct 2000 09:25:38 GMT)
Organization: ---
NNTP-Posting-Date: Mon, 23 Oct 2000 09:25:38 +0000 (UTC)
Newsgroups: comp.unix.tru64

Hi,

About a year ago I posted a question regarding getting the PC at the
time of signal reception. This did not work for me. I did not get an
answer, but now I've solved the problem myself. For your information
here it is,

Platform, OSF1 V4.0 alpha
  
Problem:

You install a signal handler to catch some signal. In the handler you
want to retrieve the value of the PC at the point of signal
reception. 

The signature of the signal handler is,

static void handler(int signo, siginfo_t* info, ucontext_t* context)

According to the documentation you can get the PC from the (ucontext_t
*) struct given to your signal handler (in context ->
uc_mcontext.sc_pc). But this is not correct. The value of context ->
uc_mcontext.sc_pc has no immediate relation to the PC.

Solution:

The value of the PC is instead,

pc = ((u_int64)info -> _sifields._sipad[25] << 32) | 
      (u_int32)info -> _sifields._sipad[24];

/Stephan



