Hi!

Our company wrote/sells a product called LOGMON to log off
idle sessions.  We have heard of people using idled although
not on Tru64 5, and it has some issues with how it determines
that a user is idle.  It uses the access time on the tty, and
so a user running a long cpu bound job with no keyboard
activity shows up as idle!

LOGMON, on the other hand, monitors the cpu usage for each
user and their child processes, so we can be sure a user
really is idle.  You can vary the inactivity time by user,
time of day, etc.  And you can control how the user is logged
off, including variations for different applications.

If this is of interest, send a message to logmon@computron.com
or visit http://www.logmon.com/ne for details  Thanks!

