I would tend to agree that sudo gives you more, at least on V4 systems.
As for dop being supported, only very partially in 4.0f, however in 5.0 and
above it is fully supported and documented. You can read the docs for it
in the usual places (Can't remember the link, but it's easy to find if you
follow the links from www.tru64.org).
It doesn't quite do the same as sudo in that if a user is permitted to run
a command then they will be able to run it with no password prompt, if they
don't have express permission then they will be prompted for the root password.
This is slightly less secure than sudo if your users are in the habit of leaving
things logged in.
From the documentation I've seen, dop will become more and more a feature of
the OS and the enhanced security system.
I wouldn't recommend using it on a 4.x system but I would recommend upgrading to
5.x and using it there.
