What did you do exactly? If you boot genvmunix after the hardware
installation, then the KZPBA should be recognized by doconfig. On our
AS1000A we had to mess around with the configuration file because some
graphics adapter that is not installed in the system showed up in the
config file. We simply deleted the corresponding line, and afterwards
the driver for the installed graphics adapter was correctly built into
the kernel.
If there is no driver for your graphics card in the kernel, then the
system should take you to a text-mode login prompt. Then you can install
the Open3D software which includes a kernel driver for your 4D50T (at
least V4.6, V4.9 and V4.92 do). Part of the post-installation procedure
of the "DWS Open3D PowerStorm 4D40T/4D50T/4D51T/4D60T V4.9-1" package is
an automated kernel build.
This was the procedure that worked on a AS1000A (installation of a
second KZPBA) and on a 
DPWS500au (okay, that was a 4D60T). I don't see any reason that these
two options cannot be installed into one workstation.

HTH,
Ralf



