Hi Henry,

You've posted only a subset of the total parameter list, so I'll make
recommendations on those.

PARAMETER                     CURRENT  NEW
----------------------------- -------  ----
ubc-minpercent                10       1
ubc-maxpercent                100      4
ubc-borrowpercent             20       2
vm-ubcseqstartpercent         50       3
vm-ubcseqpercent              10       2
maxusers                      32       256 or even 512

The "mystery parameters" you asked about in another thread are located
in the system configuration file as noted by sys_check.  On a system
named, for example, republic.usa.ibm.net, the system configuration file
would be /sys/conf/REPUBLIC.

You have set your address space and data size params to more than the
amount of physical memory you have.  I've never run a system in this
way; I've never set this parameter to more than the actual physical
memory present in the box.  The implication in what you are doing is
that you encourage your program to use swap space as program memory.
This is highly-irregular.  I would think the results of such would be
unpredictable at best, although I'll be the first to admit I am not a
programmer.



