Hi Richard,

One way would be to run the collect/collgui tool available at:

	ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/collect/

Gather your stats with "collect" while the system is doing its thing, ^C
it as soon as you believe you've enough of a sample, and use collgui to
examine the output file.  Collgui has a "processes" section that enables
you to look at what each process is using for memory at any given
collect sample interval.  It's pretty slick and I use it a lot, but more
for understanding CPU consumption and disk queues (for which the tool is
excellent, too!)

Good luck,
WJD

p.s.  Don't forget to drop those UBC and AdvFS buffers if you don't
really need 'em!


