I don't remember any method to clone a single disk of a raid set. Dumping or
vdumping file systems
disk-to-disk is possible (man restore for instructions).

> Is there a problem removing the disks and swapping them for the cloned
> disks, as far as
> the raid metadata which is stored on the originals?

With swxcr controllers the metadata is written on disks, so if you find a
way to perfectly clone all disks
"as they as", swapping the all raidset there will be no problems.
(theorically)

