Hmmmm, someone else just emailed me a similar question...  Maybe this
is why I had trouble finding info on it also!

There seems to be no man page on it, but the files are present on our
4.0C and 4.0F systems (but not on an older version 3.2 system).  See
/usr/sbin/dop and /etc/doprc.  VERY briefly, dop lets an "ordinary"
user execute a privileged command.  So, as an ordinary user, I can't
run the uerf utility, but if root makes the appropriate entry in doprc,
I can run this command by entering "dop uerf".  I learned the above
from a simple search on the web -- but even then, there wasn't too much
info.  It seems to be used by the sysman script.


